This is DEALOS, a deal-management SaaS for content creators. Full spec: FEATURE_SPEC.md. Build progress/context: PROGRESS.md — read both before any task.

STACK: Next.js 14 App Router (TS) + Tailwind + shadcn/ui frontend; NestJS (TS) + Prisma + PostgreSQL + Redis + BullMQ backend; Claude API for AI features; AWS deployment target.

CODE STANDARDS:
- TypeScript strict mode, no `any`
- Feature-based module structure (modules/deals, modules/contracts, etc.)
- DTOs + Zod/class-validator on every input
- Repository pattern over Prisma for services
- ESLint + Prettier enforced; Husky pre-commit (lint + type-check + test)
- Conventional Commits
- Centralized error handling, structured logging (pino)
- Unit tests (Jest) for all services, integration tests (Supertest) for APIs
- OpenAPI/Swagger docs for every endpoint

SECURITY (non-negotiable on every endpoint/feature):
- Ownership checks on every query (no IDOR)
- Input validation/sanitization on all DTOs
- Rate limiting on auth, AI, and public endpoints
- httpOnly secure cookies for sessions; signed time-limited JWTs for brand portal
- File upload: type/size validation, S3 SSE-KMS storage, signed URLs
- Audit log for contract, invoice, and portal actions
- No secrets in code — env vars only, documented in .env.example
- CSP, HSTS, CORS allowlist, CSRF protection on forms

FRONTEND STANDARDS:
- Consistent design tokens (Tailwind theme), dark/light mode
- Loading skeletons, empty states, error boundaries, toast notifications
- Smooth transitions (Framer Motion), mobile-responsive, accessible (ARIA, keyboard nav, contrast)

WORKFLOW: At the end of every task, append a "## Phase X Summary" section to PROGRESS.md documenting: files/modules created or changed, new API routes, Prisma schema changes, key component names, Claude prompt templates used (if any), and TODOs/decisions for the next phase. Be specific with file paths.

DESIGN: Read DESIGN_SYSTEM.md before building any UI. Apply its dark/purple theme, card styles, typography, and component patterns consistently across all pages — Dashboard, Kanban, Rate Intelligence, Contracts, Invoices, Brand Portal, etc. Maintain WCAG AA contrast in dark mode.


CODE STANDARDS - No dead code, unused imports/variables, commented-out code, or console.log in committed code
- No silent stubs/placeholders — if something can't be completed, implement a working minimal version and document the gap explicitly in PROGRESS.md under "Phase X TODOs"